    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. i'm a bit worried about the mental side of it though. sometimes when i'm in the middle of a set i just feel this weird mental block or like my brain is telling me to just give up before i actually reach my limit. how do i deal with that mental fatigue or that feeling that i'm just not up to it that day?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling is completely normal; it's often called \"hitting the wall\" and is a mental battle as much as a physical one. When that thought arises, take a deliberate 3-second pause before your next repetition and take a deep breath in and out. Visualize successfully completing the remaining reps to help refocus your intent on the goal, not the discomfort. Remember that every time you push past that urge, you build mental resilience alongside physical strength.",
      "source": "target",
